WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:20.215
"Calm down, please, Mr. Fleming. Come with me." Mr. Beck stood up.

2
00:00:20.216 --> 00:00:22.233
"You kids should run along."

3
00:00:22.234 --> 00:00:28.318
The secretary led the older man away. Henry and Maggie wandered outside.

4
00:00:28.319 --> 00:00:33.660
"That was weird," Maggie said. "Mr. Fleming seemed really mad.

5
00:00:33.661 --> 00:00:37.713
Maybe he's the one who made the threatening comment on the website!"

6
00:00:37.714 --> 00:00:42.090
"That's exactly what I was thinking." Henry frowned.

7
00:00:42.091 --> 00:00:45.902
"But why would he steal Mrs. Sweet's candy?

8
00:00:45.903 --> 00:00:53.076
And if he left that comment, why would he delete it if he's still mad?"

9
00:00:53.077 --> 00:00:57.845
"I don't know," Maggie said. "We should tell Jackson about this, though.

10
00:00:57.846 --> 00:01:02.109
Maybe he can figure it out." She looked at the town clock.

11
00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:05.612
"It's getting late. We need to finish our float."

12
00:01:05.613 --> 00:01:08.444
"Okay, let's go," Henry said.

13
00:01:08.445 --> 00:01:12.412
"We'll tell Jackson about Mr. Fleming the next time we see him."

14
00:01:12.413 --> 00:01:19.132
They walked back to the lemonade stand. Nathan was there with Cole.

15
00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:23.982
Henry and Maggie quickly told them what they'd found out during their trip into town.

16
00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:29.004
"I know Mr. Fleming," Cole said when they finished. "He lives on my block."

17
00:01:29.005 --> 00:01:32.426
"Is he always that cranky?" Maggie asked.

18
00:01:32.427 --> 00:01:36.356
Cole shrugged. "Yeah, he's pretty cranky.

19
00:01:36.357 --> 00:01:43.572
But my mom says he's like a yappy dog. His bark is worse than his bite."

20
00:01:43.573 --> 00:01:48.803
"Do you think he could have left that nasty website comment?" Henry asked.

21
00:01:48.804 --> 00:01:51.560
"Or stolen Mrs. Sweet's candy?"

22
00:01:51.561 --> 00:01:57.212
"I doubt he'd steal anything," Cole said. "I don't know about the comment."

23
00:01:57.213 --> 00:01:59.386
Maggie looked restless.

24
00:01:59.387 --> 00:02:04.947
"If you guys want to keep talking about this, let's do it while we work on our float," she said.

25
00:02:04.948 --> 00:02:08.068
"Nathan, can you watch the lemonade stand?"

26
00:02:08.069 --> 00:02:12.610
Nathan agreed, and The Lemonade Detectives headed into Maggie's house.

27
00:02:12.611 --> 00:02:17.251
Her father was in the backyard putting gasoline into the lawn tractor.

28
00:02:17.252 --> 00:02:20.932
"Are you ready for tomorrow, Dad?" Maggie asked.

29
00:02:20.933 --> 00:02:25.983
"Almost." Her father scratched his head. "There's just one problem.

30
00:02:25.984 --> 00:02:29.299
I've looked everywhere, but I can't find the hitch pin."

31
00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:32.507
"What's a hitch pin?" Cole asked.

32
00:02:32.508 --> 00:02:37.635
"It's the part that attaches our float to the tractor," Henry explained.

33
00:02:37.636 --> 00:02:41.329
"We'll definitely need it for the parade tomorrow.

34
00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:45.634
Maybe I should go over to Newman's Auto Shop and get another one."

35
00:02:45.635 --> 00:02:50.601
"Good idea, Henry." Maggie's dad pulled some bills out of his pocket.

36
00:02:50.602 --> 00:02:56.406
"This should be enough money to buy a new one."

37
00:02:56.407 --> 00:02:59.469
Soon Henry was biking to the auto shop.

38
00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:03.823
When he arrived, a fancy black convertible was parked out front.

39
00:03:03.824 --> 00:03:07.847
Its hood was up, and Mr. Newman was looking at the engine.

40
00:03:07.848 --> 00:03:12.776
"Hi, Mr. Newman," Henry said. "Isn't that the mayor's car?"

41
00:03:12.777 --> 00:03:14.634
Mr. Newman nodded.

42
00:03:14.635 --> 00:03:19.202
"He dropped it off for a tune-up so it will be ready for tomorrow's parade."

43
00:03:19.203 --> 00:03:24.388
Henry told Mr. Newman what he needed. Mr. Newman pointed inside.

44
00:03:24.389 --> 00:03:28.769
"My daughter is in the office," he said. "She'll help you."

45
00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:32.861
"Thanks." Henry went inside.

46
00:03:32.862 --> 00:03:36.214
He immediately recognized the girl in the office.

47
00:03:36.215 --> 00:03:42.280
"Oh, hi, Jade," he said. "I forgot that Mr. Newman is your dad."

48
00:03:42.281 --> 00:03:49.166
"Yeah, lucky me," Jade muttered. She sounded grouchy. "What do you want?"

49
00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:54.295
Henry told her. Jade grabbed a hitch pin out of a bin behind the counter.

50
00:03:54.296 --> 00:03:57.568
"Thanks," Henry said, handing her the money.

51
00:03:57.569 --> 00:04:04.583
"By the way, Snake told me your band had to drop out of the parade. Sorry about that."

52
00:04:04.584 --> 00:04:07.362
"I'm not sorry," Jade snapped.

53
00:04:07.363 --> 00:04:11.320
"Snake's the one who wanted to sign up for the parade.

54
00:04:11.321 --> 00:04:15.678
He thought being on TV would help our band get famous."

55
00:04:15.679 --> 00:04:17.956
Just then Mr. Newman entered.

56
00:04:17.957 --> 00:04:21.560
"What's taking so long?" he asked Jade with a frown.

57
00:04:21.561 --> 00:04:24.875
"You're supposed to be helping me with the mayor's car.

58
00:04:24.876 --> 00:04:29.347
I need to drop it off at the high school parking lot by the end of the day."

59
00:04:29.348 --> 00:04:35.179
"The high school parking lot?" Henry said. "Why are you taking it there?"

60
00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:39.184
Mr. Newman shrugged. "That's where the parade starts.

61
00:04:39.185 --> 00:04:45.491
I suppose the mayor wants it waiting there for him when everyone gathers for the parade tomorrow afternoon."

62
00:04:45.492 --> 00:04:48.100
"I'll be out to help you in a minute.

63
00:04:48.101 --> 00:04:52.948
I'm waiting on a customer," Jade told her father, waving toward Henry.

64
00:04:52.949 --> 00:04:58.322
"Well, stop gossiping about your silly band and finish up," Mr. Newman said.

65
00:04:58.323 --> 00:05:04.017
"Maybe you'll be a rock star someday, but for right now you have a job to do."

66
00:05:04.018 --> 00:05:08.555
"Whatever," Jade muttered. "Here's your change, Henry."

67
00:05:08.556 --> 00:05:15.488
She shoved some coins at Henry and then stomped out of the office with a scowl.

68
00:05:15.489 --> 00:05:18.890
Soon Henry was back on his bike, heading for home.

69
00:05:18.891 --> 00:05:23.155
As he passed the newspaper office, he saw Jackson near the entrance.

70
00:05:23.156 --> 00:05:26.368
"Hi there!" Henry called, stopping his bike.

71
00:05:26.369 --> 00:05:32.258
"I'm glad I ran into you. Something weird happened a little while ago."

72
00:05:32.259 --> 00:05:36.301
He told Jackson about Mr. Fleming's visit to the mayor's office.

73
00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:40.790
Jackson nodded. "Yes, I already heard about that," he said.

74
00:05:40.791 --> 00:05:47.577
"I also just heard that the mayor is seriously thinking about canceling the parade!"
